I have been going through my notes to recover some of the 5000 prompts that I lost when I deleted a GPT folder. I had almost forgotten all the cool science infographics I did.  These have been redone for GPT  2.5 

16:9, :root {
    --subject: "$magnetospheric plasma phenomenon";  
    --representation: "Ai inferred title";
}

# canvas {
    background: #020617;
}

# subject_render {
    mask-image: none;
    render-left-side: "Pure magnetohydrodynamics: frozen-in flux theorem, Alfvén velocity v_A = B/√(μ₀ρ), gradient-curvature drift equations, pitch-angle distribution plots, loss cone diagram, Kp index scale — all in luminous teal line art on deep indigo.";
    render-center: "The plasma in transit: field-aligned currents spiraling down flux tubes, mirror force reflecting particles, wave-particle interaction regions, ionospheric electrojet loops, 557.7 nm and 630 nm emission lines resolving into visible colour bands.";
    render-right-side: "Photoreal aurora: real green and crimson curtains over a snowfield, individual ray structures with vertical striations, faint purple nitrogen fringe, stars visible through the glow, cabin window reflection in the foreground, long-exposure grain.";
    transition-zone: "The loss cone diagram filling in with actual precipitating particles. The emission wavelength value becoming the colour of the sky.";
}

